{"text": "Otto Loewi was a pharmacologist whose discoveries greatly advanced the study of chemical communication between nerve cells. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Born in Frankfurt, Germany, in 1873, he originally hoped to study art history. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> However, following his parents advice, Loewi studied medicine at the University of Strasbourg, Germany now part of France. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Although he was qualified as a physician, he chose to switch from a doctor treating patients to a medical researcher seeking cures. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> In 1902, he first met Henry Dale in Ernest Starlings laboratory in London, where he spent several months. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> In 1936, he and Henry Dale shared the Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> After Germany invaded Austria in 1938, Loewi was forced to leave Austria, where he was living at the time. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Loewi became a research professor at New York Universitys College of Medicine in 1940.", "alignment": {"characters": ["O", "t", "t", "o", " ", "L", "o", "e", "w", "i", " ", "w", "a", "s", " ", "a", " ", "p", "h", "a", "r", "m", "a", "c", "o", "l", "o", "g", "i", "s", "t", " ", "w", "h", "o", "s", "e", " ", "d", "i", "s", "c", "o", "v", "e", "r", "i", "e", "s", " ", "g", "r", "e", "a", "t", "l", "y", " ", "a", "d", "v", "a", "n", "c", "e", "d", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "s", "t", "u", "d", "y", " ", "o", "f", " ", "c", "h", "e", "m", "i", "c", "a", "l", " ", "c", "o", "m", "m", "u", "n", "i", "c", "a", "t", "i", "o", "n", " ", "b", "e", "t", "w", "e", "e", "n", " ", "n", "e", "r", "v", "e", " ", "c", "e", "l", "l", "s", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "B", "o", "r", "n", " ", "i", "n", " ", "F", "r", "a", "n", "k", "f", "u", "r", "t", ",", " ", "G", "e", "r", "m", "a", "n", "y", ",", " ", "i", "n", " ", "1", "8", "7", "3", ",", " ", "h", "e", " ", "o", "r", "i", "g", "i",